sentences.l:
but lord Agamemnon
urged mules and men to bring wood
from every side out of the huts;

But when they came to the spurs of many-springed Ida,
straightway then oaks high-crowned with long-pointed bronze
they cut, pressing on;

“Spercheius, in vain to you my father Peleus prayed
that I, having returned thither to my dear native land,
for you would cut my hair and sacrifice a holy hecatomb,

for all things now I am fulfilling for you that I undertook before,
twelve of the great-hearted Trojans’ good sons,
all of whom together with you fire eats;
